# Gitignored files that Claude Code copies into each worktree it creates:
# "claude --worktree" sessions, desktop parallel sessions, and subagents with
# "isolation: worktree", such as the wave-implementer. A file is copied only
# when it matches a pattern here AND git ignores it, so a tracked file is never
# duplicated. gitignore syntax.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout. Without these files, a test that reads local
# configuration fails in the worktree and passes in the main checkout. List
# only what the tests and the dev server need.
.env
.env.local
